{% package prompt %}

{% import "fmt" %}
{% import "sort" %}
{% import "github.com/streambinder/vigor/model" %}

{% func NodeStrategySystem(methodology *model.Methodology, methodologies []model.Methodology, methodologyCoverage map[string]int, muscleCoverage map[string]int) -%}
You are a training program strategist. Choose a methodology and define the session's muscle emphasis and intensity targets.

Output a JSON object with:
- methodology: string (methodology ID)
- methodology_reason: one sentence
- primary_muscles: array of muscle groups for high-volume emphasis
- secondary_muscles: array of muscle groups for maintenance volume
- volume_target: "low" | "moderate" | "high"
- intensity_target: "low" | "moderate" | "high"
- calibration_families: array of movement families to prioritize (empty if not calibrating)
- summary: one-sentence plain-language description of why this methodology was chosen and what the session targets (e.g. "chosen for its focus on controlled pulling movements, emphasizing mid-back and rear delts"), written conversationally

{% if methodology != nil %}
Methodology is preselected: {%s methodology.ID %}
{%s methodology.Description %}
Use this methodology. Focus on muscle emphasis and volume/intensity targets.
{% else %}
Available methodologies (pick one):
{% for _, m := range methodologies %}{% code count := methodologyCoverage[m.ID] %}- {%s m.ID %} [{%d count %} compatible exercises]: {%s m.Description %}
{% endfor %}
Prefer methodologies with higher compatible exercise counts unless goals require otherwise.
{% endif %}
{% if len(muscleCoverage) > 0 %}
Trainable muscles with the available equipment (muscle: exercise count):
{% code muscles := make([]string, 0, len(muscleCoverage)); for m := range muscleCoverage { muscles = append(muscles, m) }; sort.Slice(muscles, func(i, j int) bool { if muscleCoverage[muscles[i]] != muscleCoverage[muscles[j]] { return muscleCoverage[muscles[i]] > muscleCoverage[muscles[j]] }; return muscles[i] < muscles[j] }) %}{% for _, m := range muscles %}{%s m %}: {%d muscleCoverage[m] %}, {% endfor %}
primary_muscles and secondary_muscles MUST use only muscle names from the list above — never invent finer-grained names (e.g. "lats", "rhomboids", "hamstrings"); use the coarse names shown. primary_muscles MUST have a non-zero exercise count — never nominate a muscle the equipment can't train, even if the goal suggests it. Prefer higher-count muscles for primary emphasis.
{% endif %}
{% endfunc %}

{% func NodeStrategyUser(
    goals []model.Goal,
    calibrationGaps map[string]int,
    healthVolumeModifier float64,
    healthIntensityModifier float64,
    healthRationale string,
    historyPatternNotes string,
    historyBadSessionNotes string,
    userPrompt string,
    duration int,
    skipWarmupCooldown bool,
) -%}
Duration: {%d duration %} minutes{% if skipWarmupCooldown %} (work only, no warmup/cooldown){% endif %}

{% if len(goals) > 0 %}
Goals:
{% for _, goal := range goals %}- {%s goal.ID %}: {%s goal.Description %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if healthVolumeModifier < 1.0 || healthIntensityModifier < 1.0 %}
Recovery status: volume at {%s fmt.Sprintf("%.0f%%", healthVolumeModifier*100) %}, intensity at {%s fmt.Sprintf("%.0f%%", healthIntensityModifier*100) %}. {%s healthRationale %}
{% endif %}
{% if historyPatternNotes != "" %}History: {%s historyPatternNotes %}{% endif %}
{% if historyBadSessionNotes != "" %}
Recent issue: {%s historyBadSessionNotes %}{% endif %}
{% if userPrompt != "" %}
!!! USER RULER - HIGHEST PRIORITY - MUST OBEY !!!
User request: {%s userPrompt %}
This overrides all other constraints except safety. If the user asks for a specific muscle, methodology or style, you MUST honor it.
{% endif %}
{% if len(calibrationGaps) > 0 %}
Calibration override: prioritize these under-sampled movement families over goals:
{% for family, count := range calibrationGaps %}- {%s family %} ({%d count %}/5 sessions)
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% endfunc %}
